The class `MaybeFromCompletionStage` is a thin adapter that wires a `CompletionStage` to a RxJava `Maybe`. Its logic consists mainly of reference assignments and delegating callbacks without any computationally intensive work. Such lightweight glue code generally does not warrant dedicated JMH benchmarks, as the measured overhead would be dominated by the underlying `CompletionStage` implementation and the RxJava infrastructure rather than the adapter itself. Consequently, creating a JMH benchmark would provide little actionable insight.